<h1 class="page-title">About Tico</h1>
<p class="marketing-lede">
  Confident staff make better tables. That's the whole thesis.
</p>

<section class="marketing-section">
  <p>
    Tico started from a simple observation: the gap between a staff
    member studying material and actually being ready for a real shift is
    where guest experience quietly breaks down. Menu quizzes and
    onboarding binders test recall. They don't build the confidence it
    takes to handle a real guest, in the moment, under mild pressure —
    and that confidence is what actually shows up at the table.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tico is built around two products, one thesis: <strong>make every
    ticket count.</strong> Train builds the confidence and consistency
    your staff bring to every shift. Insights shows you what's actually
    driving revenue, so you know where that training effort pays off
    most.
  </p>
  <p>
    We're early, and we'd rather be honest about that than oversell it —
    this is a small, focused product built with real restaurants, not a
    platform with a long feature list to live up to.
  </p>
</section>
